ut this seems premature as it doesn't address Black's strong d5 pawn and creates potential weaknesses.\n\nReason: I choose **P: e4-d5** because:\n- It eliminates Black's central pawn immediately\n- While Black can recapture with the queen (Qd8xd5), I can then develop with tempo by playing N: b1-c3, attacking the queen\n- This leads to a favorable version of the Scandinavian Defense reversed (since I'm White capturing on d5)\n- It simplifies the center and gives me better piece coordination opportunities\n- The alternative d2-d4 allows Black to maintain central tension with options like dxe4 or maintaining the pawn\n\nAnswer: P: e4-d5"}
