 knight for a pawn.\n\nReason: Capturing the knight on c6 with d5-c6 wins significant material (a knight is worth approximately 3 pawns). This is a clear tactical win that immediately gives White a substantial advantage. In chess, when you can win material cleanly, it's almost always the right choice, especially a whole piece.\n\nAnswer: P: d5-c6"}
