Queen away from h4 but weakens my kingside significantly, creating dark square weaknesses around my King.\n\n5. **N: g1-e2** - Defends f4 and prepares to address the Queen threat, but is more passive than f3.\n\nReason:\nN: g1-f3 is the strongest move because it:\n- Develops a knight to its natural square\n- Directly attacks the threatening Black Queen on h4\n- Prepares for kingside castling\n- Follows classical opening principles (develop pieces, control center)\n- Forces Black's Queen to retreat, losing time\n- Maintains a solid pawn structure\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
