se and puts it on the rim, very passive.\n\n**Reason:**\nThe black queen on h4 is my most pressing problem. I need to force it to retreat while maintaining defensive solidity. Playing g2-g3 accomplishes multiple objectives:\n- Forces the black queen to move from its threatening position\n- Opens the g-file for potential future play\n- Maintains my knight's strong position on f3\n- Creates luft for my king\n\nWhile g2-g3 does create slight dark-square weaknesses, the tactical necessity of pushing back Black's queen outweighs this structural concern. After the queen moves, I can focus on completing development and castling.\n\n**Answer:** P: g2-g3"}
