tical threats\n- The knight on e5 is well-supported and can coordinate with my other pieces\n\nReason: With Black's king on c8 and somewhat exposed, I want to increase pressure and activity. The knight on e5 is a powerful centralized piece that restricts Black's options and prepares for further tactical opportunities. This move develops my position actively while maintaining threats against Black's somewhat unsafe king position.\n\nAnswer: N: f3-e5"}
