. Looking more carefully, I should secure my king's safety first while maintaining piece activity.\n\nReason: Castling kingside (K: e1-g1) is the principled move. Despite Black's queen being on h4, castling accomplishes several goals:\n1. Improves king safety by moving off the central files\n2. Connects my rooks\n3. Activates the h1 rook\n4. After castling, I can defend with moves like f2-f3 or h2-h3 to control the queen's influence\n\nThis is a fundamental principle - getting the king to safety and developing pieces takes priority in the opening/middlegame.\n\nAnswer: K: e1-g1"}
