 king to move immediately\n- It attacks the rook on e8 simultaneously (a royal fork pattern)\n- After the king moves (likely Kb8, Kd8, or Kb7), I can capture the rook with Nxe8, winning significant material\n- This is a classic knight fork tactic - attacking king and rook at the same time\n- Black cannot ignore the check, so the rook is lost\n\nAnswer: N: e5-d7"}
