e strongest move. It gives check to the Black king on c8, which is a forcing move that Black must respond to immediately. The king will likely have to move to b8, b7, or d8, and all of these squares worsen Black's king position. Additionally, the knight on b6 would be well-placed, controlling important central squares and potentially supporting further attacks. Forcing moves that improve my position while worsening my opponent's are generally the best choices.\n\nAnswer: N: d7-b6"}
