n c7 and Rook on e8.\n\nReason: **N: b6-d7** is the strongest move because:\n1. It forks the Black Rook on e8 and Knight on f5\n2. Black must respond to save the Rook (likely Re8-e7 or another square)\n3. After Black moves the Rook, I can capture the Knight on f5 (Nd7xf5)\n4. This wins material (a Knight) while maintaining pressure\n5. It's a forcing move that seizes the initiative\n\nAnswer: N: b6-d7"}
