 g3-g4**: Attacks the knight on f5 but allows Black time to consolidate.\n\nReason: B: e8-d7 is clearly the strongest move. It delivers check to Black's exposed king on c8, forcing Black to respond to the threat immediately. This gains tempo and disrupts Black's coordination. After the king moves, I can continue to apply pressure with my well-placed bishop. Forcing moves that put the opponent's king in check are typically strong when available, and this fits perfectly with the principle of maintaining initiative.\n\nAnswer: B: e8-d7"}
