ck's rook on b5 would need to deal with this threat, but it's difficult to stop a pawn on e6 without the king's help.\n\nReason: Pushing e5-e6 creates an unstoppable passed pawn threat. Black's king on a7 cannot reach the pawn in time, and the rook alone will struggle to stop it while I have two bishops to support the advance. This is the most direct path to victory - advancing the passed pawn with tempo.\n\nAnswer: P: e5-e6"}
