 e6 pawn is my most dangerous asset. Advancing it to e7 puts enormous pressure on Black, forcing their pieces to react. With the Black king on a7 and rook on b5, they cannot immediately prevent e7-e8=Q on my next turn unless the rook moves to e5 or the king somehow gets closer (which is impossible in one move). This is a forcing move that puts Black in a critical defensive position.\n\nAnswer: P: e6-e7"}
