ending the king's position), after the king moves, the knight will likely be hanging or I'll have won crucial tempo. This forcing check disrupts Black's coordination and puts me in a commanding position. In rook endgames, activity and forcing moves are critical, and this move accomplishes both objectives immediately.\n\nAnswer: R: b1-b6"}
