ishop controlling key squares and the Black king on b7 being the only piece that can potentially stop it, this pawn will tie down Black's forces. Combined with White's extra bishop and material advantage, this should lead to a straightforward win. The pawn can advance with bishop support while the king comes up to help.\n\nAnswer: P: c2-c4"}
