s. Moving K: h5-h6 directly supports advancing the h4 pawn next turn (if I get it), brings my King closer to promotion, and maintains pressure. The Black King on a8 is far from stopping my h-pawn, and my Bishop can help control key squares while also potentially dealing with Black's a-pawns.\n\nAnswer: K: h5-h6"}
