 of Black's King. With the Bishop on b6, the Black King cannot escape via b6 or c5, forcing it into a smaller box. This allows me to bring my Knight from h6 via efficient routes to deliver checkmate in coordination with the Bishop. The move also prevents any counterplay Black might have with the a4 pawn since I maintain control of critical squares.\n\nAnswer: B: c7-b6"}
